# The `busybox` producer: the `mica-busybox` package -- ONE emergency binary at
# /usr/bin/busybox, with no applet links, no PATH entry and no unit.
#
# Plain `KEY=value` lines only: no logic, no command substitution, no
# expansion. Safe to source from bash and to parse with grep/sed from anything
# else, and checked for that shape by build-env/deb/build.sh before it is
# sourced. build-env/deb/README.md documents every field.

PACKAGES="mica-busybox"

# `amd64 arm64` and NOT `all`. The payload is one dynamically linked ELF, so
# there is an architecture in it and dpkg-shlibdeps has to resolve its libc
# against the architecture it will run on. That is also why the harvest stage
# below runs at the TARGET platform: build.sh sets BUILD_PLATFORM from --arch,
# so `--arch arm64` unpacks the arm64 archive and packs it in the arm64 packer.
ARCHES="amd64 arm64"

# The pinned Debian trixie base the harvest stage downloads from, resolved by
# the driver through build-env/from.sh so that this producer stands on the same
# digest the rest of the tree does. It is the same base
# rootfs/compose/10-compose.Dockerfile assembles the device root from, which is
# what makes the harvested binary's libc the one it will link against on the
# device.
FROM_IMAGES="MOS_IMAGE_DEBIAN_TRIXIE=IMAGE_DEBIAN_TRIXIE"

# NO `family` context, and the omission is a decision. The shared
# rootfs/packages-src/copyright is for payloads THIS REPOSITORY WROTE and says
# so in its own Comment; this payload is Debian's busybox binary, byte for byte,
# under GPL-2. The Dockerfile therefore harvests busybox's own copyright and the
# GPL-2 text it points at, and composes the shipped copyright out of those.
# Using the Apache file here would be a licence statement that is simply untrue.

# No unit, no wants-symlink, nothing enabled. That is the WHOLE POINT of this
# package: an emergency binary that anything started automatically would have
# stopped being an emergency binary. Written as an explicit zero for the reason
# every zero here is -- an omission and a deliberate zero look identical, and
# only one of them is a decision.
ENABLEMENT="mica-busybox=0"
